OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Thu 5 Nov to Sat 14 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure will dominate across the
OL,7,FUK early in this period, bringing a
OL,8,Flot of dry weather. Some places may
OL,9,Fstart foggy, mainly in the north, this
OL,10,Fslow to clear and possibly even
OL,11,Flingering all day. Elsewhere, cloud
OL,12,Famounts will be variable, but there
OL,13,Fshould be some sunshine. Cloud is
OL,14,Flikely to be thick enough at times for
OL,15,Fa few mainly light showers or some
OL,16,Fdrizzle though. For most, temperatures
OL,17,Fare likely to be close to normal,
OL,18,Fthough it will be chilly where any fog
OL,19,Flingers, and in the breezier south.
OL,20,FSome overnight frost is likely where
OL,21,Fskies are clear and winds remain
OL,22,Flight. As we head into the following
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fweek, there are signs that more
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Funsettled but potentially milder
OL,25,Fweather may return, but confidence
OL,26,Fsurrounding this change is low.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
